option.AURELIA_ADAPTIVE.comment=Smooths prior-frame time with slow recovery. Master switch for Adaptive shadow filtering, its only consumer; off means a fixed shadow filter.
option.AURELIA_SHADOWS.comment=Reload-bound. Potato disables the map completely.
option.AURELIA_SHADOW_RESOLUTION.comment=Reload-bound square depth allocation. Adaptive keeps this allocation fixed.
option.AURELIA_SHADOW_DISTANCE.comment=Reload-bound caster and receiver coverage distance in blocks.
option.AURELIA_SHADOW_FILTER_MAX.comment=Shadow-map reads use hardware-compared filtering. 1 takes one filtered read, 2 takes two (smoother diagonal edges), 3 takes four (a softer tent), dropping to two or one while Adaptive shadow filtering is short of frame-time headroom.
option.AURELIA_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=Only attenuates direct sunlight; cool ambient and block light stay visible.
option.AURELIA_SHADOW_ADAPTIVE.comment=Adaptive profile only. Only matters at Maximum shadow filter 3. Uses the smoothed frame-time signal to choose between one and four filtered reads without resizing the map.
option.AURELIA_WATER_SURFACE.comment=Analytic water: wave-perturbed normal, Fresnel, sky reflection and a sun glint. No extra texture and no extra render target. Potato disables it; turning it off restores the plain gbuffers_terrain appearance of water.
option.AURELIA_WATER_ANIMATED.comment=Two travelling analytic waves move the water normal with time so the surface breathes instead of sitting still. ALU only, no texture or render target; Potato and Low disable it.
option.AURELIA_WATER_DEPTH.comment=One depthtex1 read (the pre-translucent opaque depth) gives the water column thickness: shallow water reads clearer, deep water settles to the accepted blue palette. One depth fetch and a few ALU ops; only the water body colour changes, so Fresnel, reflection and glint are unaffected. Potato and Low disable it.
option.AURELIA_WATER_SHORE.comment=Reuses the depth-tinted water's thickness signal to fade the water's opacity, and ease its reflection weight, as the column thins toward the waterline, so shallow water dissolves into the floor instead of ending on a hard edge. No foam, no wave change, no extra texture read and no extra pass. Potato and Low disable it.
option.AURELIA_WATER_UNDERWATER.comment=When the camera is submerged, terrain, water, weather and clouds fade toward a palette-derived water colour on a denser fog curve, the vertical term reads brighter upward, and the sky background becomes the same colour. Reuses the existing fog contract; no extra pass, render target, noise or texture read. Potato and Low disable it.
option.AURELIA_ATMOSPHERE.comment=Analytic atmosphere: a directional sky gradient, sun/moon glow and a weather response, all ALU only with no extra texture or render target. Potato disables it; turning it off restores the flat analytical sky.
option.AURELIA_CLOUDS_SOFT.comment=Dissolved cloud edges, denser-core shading, a warm sun-side rim at low sun and a darker desaturated rain response, all ALU only on the vanilla cloud slab. Potato keeps the simplest treatment.
option.AURELIA_EXPOSURE.comment=Scene exposure applied before the filmic curve. 1.00 is the neutral baseline; higher values brighten the whole image.
option.AURELIA_CONTRAST.comment=Micro-contrast applied about mid-grey after the filmic curve. 1.00 is the neutral baseline; higher values deepen shadows and lift highlights.
option.AURELIA_DEBUG_VIEW.comment=Lighting shows normal and lightmap data. Frame pacing shows red pressure, green quality, blue reference. Raw shadow map displays depth. Shadow factor displays applied direct-light visibility. Adaptive shadow quality: red, amber, green are the low, middle and top adaptive tiers; only the top tier takes four reads (at Maximum shadow filter 3).
option.AURELIA_DISTANT_RAIN.comment=EXPERIMENTAL, off in every preset: adds a procedural two-layer distant-rain curtain on the final pass. Native Minecraft weather already surrounds the player, so this stays an experiment for manual testing only.
option.AURELIA_DISTANT_RAIN_LAYERS.comment=EXPERIMENTAL: number of curtain layers when the distant-rain curtain is enabled. 1 is cheapest, 2 is the tuned default.
option.AURELIA_FOLIAGE_TRANSLUCENCY.comment=Wrapped transmission for thin geometry: leaves and grass facing away from the sun pick up a little sunlight when you look sunward, instead of going black. Costs a few ALU ops and no texture read; it does not touch the shadow term.
option.AURELIA_WETNESS_SPECULAR.comment=A small Blinn highlight that fades in with rain strength and is off in dry weather, so rain reads as wet surfaces. ALU only, no extra texture or render target.
profile.comment=Potato disables shadows, sky treatment, water effects and soft clouds. Low is a 512 map at 64 blocks with the water surface only. Balanced targets the M1 Air with a 1024 map at 96 blocks and every water effect. Cinematic uses a 1536 map at 128 blocks with the four-read shadow filter. Adaptive keeps a 1024 map fixed and changes only the shadow filter budget.
